results.statement:
Let $\Phi_{\mathrm{dBN}}$ be the de Bruijn Newman kernel, the even function with $H_t(z)=\int_{\mathbb{R}}
u_t(u)e^{izu}\,du$, $
u_t(u)= rac12\Phi_{\mathrm{dBN}}(u)e^{tu^2}$, and let $L_{n,t}$ be the Laguerre expressions of $H_t$ of the book, so that $L_{n,t}(x)/L_{n,t}(0)=\mathbb{E}_{n,t}\cos(xw)$, where under $\mathbb{E}_{n,t}$ the pair $(u,v)$ has the density proportional to $b^{2n}
u_t(u)
u_t(v)$, where $b=u-v$ and $w=u+v$. Then $\lim_{n	o\infty}\sup_{0\le t\le1/2}\mathbb{E}_{n,t}[w^2]=0$. Consequently, for every $X<\infty$ there is $N_X$ with $L_{n,t}(x)>0$ for all $n\ge N_X$, $|x|\le X$ and $0\le t\le rac12$. The index $N_X$ is not effective. The result is due to Newton (2026, Zenodo).
